    'Picture a Mexican wave in a stadium: the crowd rises and sits (the disturbance) and the wave travels around the stands, but no person moves to the next seat. An electromagnetic wave is similar — a wiggle of electric and magnetic fields travels through space, but no matter moves along with it. The electric wiggle and the magnetic wiggle stand up straight, side by side at right angles, while the wave runs forward. Because the wiggles make each other, the wave can cross empty space with nothing to push — that is why sunlight reaches us through the vacuum of space.',
