      correction:
        'In phase means both fields reach maxima/minima at the same space-time points. It does NOT mean their numerical values are equal. The amplitudes are related by E₀/B₀ = c, so for typical light E₀ ≈ 100 V/m while B₀ ≈ 3.3×10⁻⁷ T.',
    },
    {
      belief: 'Different regions of the EM spectrum travel at different speeds in vacuum.',
