        'A microwave oven operates at f = 2.45 GHz. Calculate its wavelength λ in cm (to 1 decimal place, e.g. 12.2). Then state which device produces these waves.',
      answer: '12.2',
      answerType: 'text',
      unit: 'cm',
      formula: 'λ = c/f',
      working: 'λ = c/f = 3e8 / 2.45e9 = 0.122 m = 12.2 cm. Produced by a magnetron.',
